{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You’re here because of abdominal pain and nausea again, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. It’s the same pain I always get. I couldn’t keep anything down. I was only home one day last time and it came right back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you’re saying this feels like your usual gastroparesis flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I haven’t had a bowel movement in a week. I’m in so much pain. I just want it to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:06:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ve reviewed your records. You’ve been through this many times. We’ll start with IV fluids and medications to help with nausea and pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:07:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But last time, Reglan didn’t help. They switched me to promethazine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. We’re not using Reglan this time because it didn’t work before. We’re giving you promethazine and another anti-nausea med as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:09:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And can you do something for the pain? It’s really bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re giving you tramadol and Tylenol regularly, and dilaudid for breakthrough pain through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:11:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My blood pressure was high too when I came in, wasn’t it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your systolic was 253. We’ve increased your nifedipine from 60 to 90 mg daily. That should help bring it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:13:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on that for years. It’s hard to keep it under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2145-05-31 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. Pain and stress can make it worse. As your pain improves, your pressure should too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2145-05-31 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We placed a central line in your neck because your veins are hard to access. It’ll help with giving meds and fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2145-05-31 16:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had those before. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2145-05-31 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s routine. We did a chest X-ray to make sure it’s in the right place. No complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2145-06-01 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your kidney function was a bit off when you came in—creatinine was 1.4—but it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2145-06-01 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the diabetes? I’ve had protein in my urine before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2145-06-01 08:17:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely. We call it diabetic kidney disease. Your current kidney issue is acute but related to dehydration and the flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2145-06-01 08:18:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it get better?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2145-06-01 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it already is. Your creatinine is down to 1.0 today. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One thing—we saw a mild elevation in your white blood cell count, 18.5, but that’s been high before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. It’s been high in past records. We call it chronic leukocytosis. No fever or other signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But you did a blood culture, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. One culture showed a small amount of coagulase-negative staph, but it’s likely a contaminant since only one bottle grew it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:05:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I don’t need antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2145-06-01 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We gave one dose of daptomycin just in case, but since you’re not sick and repeat cultures are negative, we’re not continuing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2145-06-01 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine test showed white blood cells, but no bacteria grew. You don’t have symptoms of a UTI, so we’re not treating it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2145-06-01 10:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I’ve had so many UTIs because of the diverticulum. Shouldn’t I get something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2145-06-01 10:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand, but treating without symptoms could lead to resistance. We’ll repeat the urine test as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2145-06-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is coming down—now 10.3. That supports it was stress-related, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2145-06-02 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s because of the pain and gastroparesis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2145-06-02 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely. But we’ll suggest your primary doctor look into it further, maybe with a hematology consult."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2145-06-03 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing better. You’ve been able to eat soft foods and keep them down. That’s great progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2145-06-03 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still nauseous sometimes, but not vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2145-06-03 09:17:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the prochlorperazine suppository available. The promethazine by mouth is helping too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2145-06-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We consulted GI. They agree this is a gastroparesis flare. They recommend a gastric emptying study to confirm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2145-06-03 14:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had scopes before. Will I need one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2145-06-03 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, tomorrow. An EGD to check your stomach. It’s mostly to rule out other causes, like ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The EGD is done. Good news—no ulcers or blockages. The stomach looked a bit pale with mild redness, but nothing serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I threw up a lot before the test. Was that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:02:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s common with severe gastroparesis. They had to intubate you briefly for safety, but you’re okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep advancing your diet. For the gastric emptying study, you’ll need to stop pain meds like tramadol first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the pain comes back if I stop them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2145-06-04 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. That’s why GI may consider other options like domperidone, which isn’t used often but can help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Your pain is much better, labs are improved, and you’re eating. We’d like to send you home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:01:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue insulin, sertraline, gabapentin, and pantoprazole. Nifedipine is now 90 mg daily. We’re keeping tramadol and promethazine for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the iron pills? They upset my stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noted that. Ask your doctor about IV iron—it avoids the stomach and might be easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:05:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the port? I keep needing lines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve referred you for evaluation. If you keep getting admitted, a port could make things easier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:07:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your primary doctor and GI soon. They’ll arrange the gastric study and review your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:09:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just want to get better. I’m tired of being sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2145-06-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hear you. We’ll work with your team to find better long-term solutions. For now, rest and follow the plan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2145-06-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge papers are ready. We’re updating your nifedipine and keeping your pain and nausea meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2145-06-05 10:31:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel better than I have in weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2145-06-05 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if things worsen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final note—your blood sugar was high on admission, around 350. Keeping it controlled helps prevent these flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I try, but when I’m sick, it’s hard to eat right or stay on schedule."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. That’s why follow-up is so important. Maybe diabetes education can help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:03:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll add that to your referrals. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2145-06-05 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2145-05-31 15:02:00",
    "admission_end": "2145-06-05 15:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 2 diabetes, gastroparesis, and recurrent UTIs due to urethral diverticulum was admitted for acute-on-chronic abdominal pain consistent with a gastroparesis flare. She presented with nausea, vomiting, and inability to tolerate oral intake, along with severe pain and elevated blood pressure. IV fluids, antiemetics, and pain management with tramadol, Tylenol, and dilaudid were initiated. A central line was placed due to poor venous access. Hypertension was managed by increasing nifedipine to 90 mg daily. Blood cultures showed a single positive for coagulase-negative staph, deemed a contaminant; no ongoing antibiotics were given. Urinalysis showed pyuria but no growth, and no treatment was initiated. An EGD revealed mild gastric erythema but no ulcers or obstruction. Her symptoms improved, she advanced to a soft diet, and was discharged home with medication adjustments and plans for outpatient follow-up with primary care and gastroenterology, including a gastric emptying study and evaluation for a port and IV iron.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Body Mass Index 45.0-49.9, adult",
      "Peripheral autonomic neuropathy in disorders classified elsewhere",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Obesity, unspecified",
      "Other specified disease of white blood cells",
      "Other nonspecific findings on examination of urine",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Personal history, urinary (tract) infection",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health"
    ]
  }
}
